#
# Settings of the kernel and of extensions that compose.yaml does not name (MK-129). Copy this file
# to mosaikit.env, which Docker Compose passes to the mosaikit service, and restart it:
#
#   docker compose up -d mosaikit
#
# One VARIABLE=value per line: the name of the setting in upper case, with every character that is
# not a letter or a digit replaced by "_" (example.reports.endpoint is EXAMPLE_REPORTS_ENDPOINT).
# Keep mosaikit.env out of version control and readable only by the account that runs Docker: it may
# hold passwords. To keep secret settings in a file of their own, see README.md.

# A setting of an extension, here the address of the service of an example extension.
#EXAMPLE_REPORTS_ENDPOINT=https://reports.example.org

# A setting of the kernel, such as how long a session lasts without activity.
#MOSAIKIT_ACCOUNTS_SESSION_TIMEOUT=4h

# Cookies of the kernel always Secure, for an installation reached only over HTTPS.
#MOSAIKIT_ACCOUNTS_SECURE_COOKIES=true
